This file's mere presence disables Jekyll processing on GitHub Pages.
It matters only if this site is ever published from a branch (e.g. main /(root))
instead of via the GitHub Actions artifact deployment used currently.
Its content is ignored by GitHub — it only checks that the file exists.

Why it is needed: site/_2026_and_you_get_a_canton,_everybody_gets_a_canton!.html
starts with an underscore, and Jekyll silently skips any file or directory
whose name begins with "_" or ".".
